{{Term/Store|Ravio's Hood||Series, BotW, TotK}},<ref name="BotW Inventory"/><ref name="TotK Inventory"/> also known as the '''Rabbit Hood''',{{Exp Game|HWL}}{{Name Ref|HWL}} is a recurring [[Item]] in {{TLoZ Series}}. Ravio's Hood goes unnamed in {{ALBW}} and {{HW}}.

==Location and Uses==
==={{ALBW|-}}===
Ravio's Hood is a piece of clothing worn by [[Ravio]] in {{ALBW}}. It is worn to mask his identity as [[Link]]'s [[Lorule]]an counterpart. Ravio removes his Hood after Link defeats [[Yuga Ganon]], pleading for [[Hilda]] to give up her attempt to steal [[Hyrule]]'s [[Triforce]].<ref name="ALBW Ravio"/>

==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Descriptions BotW}}
Ravio's Hood is a piece of [[Armor]] introduced in the "[[EX Treasure: Merchant Hood]]" [[Side Quest]] from {{TCB}} [[Downloadable Content]] pack in {{BotW}}. It is a priceless relic that was once kept safely within the walls of [[Hyrule Castle (Dungeon)|Hyrule Castle]], but was later stolen by [[Misko]]. Misko hints at the whereabouts of Ravio's Hood in [[Misko's EX Journal 2]] in the [[Deya Village Ruins]],<ref name="BotW Misko's EX Journal 2"/> claiming that it rests in the right hand of a dragon near [[Dracozu Lake]].<ref name="BotW Misko's EX Journal 2 2"/> The [[Treasure Chest]] housing Ravio's Hood can be found embedded in the ground beneath the right hand of the dragon statue at the [[Spring of Courage]]. In order to retrieve it, Link must use the [[Magnesis]] [[Rune]] to pull it from the ground.

Ravio's Hood is the same Hood worn by [[Ravio]].<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> When worn, it grants Link the [[Sideways Climbing Speed Increased]] [[Added Effect]], which increases his sideways [[Climbing]] speed. If Link sells Ravio's Hood, he can later purchase it from [[Granté]] at [[Tarrey Town]] for 50 [[Rupee]]s. Ravio's Hood cannot be enhanced by a [[Great Fairy]], nor can it be [[Dye]]d at the [[Kochi Dye Shop]].

